#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""herd -- ask another agent in this Emacs's herd, or answer an ask.

Usage:
  herd ask TO [TEXT|-] [--wait] [--timeout SECS] [--rounds N]
  herd handoff PROJECT [TEXT|-] [--wait] [--timeout SECS] [--rounds N]
  herd reply ID [TEXT|-]
  herd status ID
  herd cancel ID
  herd relay TARGET [KIND] [--reason TEXT]
  herd start KIND [--worktree [BRANCH] | --no-worktree] [--name NAME] [--notes TEXT] [--new]
  herd stop NAME
  herd list
  herd asks
  herd remember [--type T] [--name SLUG] [--new] [--user|--project P] [TEXT|-]
  herd recall [--user|--project P] [QUERY...]
  herd search WORDS... | --session ID [--at TURN]
  herd forget [--user|--project P] NAME
  herd promote propose --fact NAME... --file PATH [--project P]   (diff on stdin)
  herd promote propose --fact NAME --lint [--user|--project P]    (the rule on stdin)
  herd lint check [--rule FILE] [--cwd DIR] [COMMAND|-]
  herd lint                        (a CLI's PreToolUse hook on a shell call)
  herd hook [EVENT]                (from a CLI's lifecycle hook)
  herd hooks install|uninstall|status [--dry-run]
  herd hooks list [--json] [--project DIR]...
  herd cost [--days N] [--project P] [--tasks] [--json]

TO is an agent's name, or a kind -- claude, grok, agy -- to take that
kind's agent in your project.  TEXT `-', or left out, reads stdin.

`ask' without --wait prints the ask's id and returns; the answer comes
back to you as a message once you are idle.  With --wait it prints the
answer itself when it arrives.  Run that in the background if your CLI
can: you are told when it finishes.

Rounds: while it answers your ask, its taker may ask any one agent N
times at most -- --rounds N, 5 when not given; past that the herd
refuses, and the taker answers you with where it stands.  You are held
to the same with each agent you ask: for the ask you are answering, or,
asked by nobody, until you finish a turn with no ask open.

`handoff' hands work to another project's lead, when what you found
needs a change there: do not edit its checkout yourself.  PROJECT is a
path, or the leaf name (unnoiac) or slug of a project the herd knows --
one with agents, a memory store, or that claude has run in.  Brief it as you would
an ask: what you found, the evidence (files, logs, tickets, commits),
what is needed, when it is done, and who waits on it.  It is an ask --
the answer, --wait, --rounds and the loop rules are an ask's -- and the
herd frames it for that lead: from which project and agent, that you
wait on it, what to do with it.  A project with no lead gets one started
there, if the herd is set to and it is a git checkout.  A project's lead
may hand off, and so may an agent in a project with no lead; an agent
working under a lead is refused -- it puts what the other project needs
in its answer to its lead, which hands it off.

`cost' compares what a task costs, in weighted tokens (input 1, cache
read 0.1, cache write 1.25 or 2, output 5), through a lead and talking to
an agent directly, over the last N local days (7; at most 30): the
tasks, the median and total per task, the median of those that changed
code, the tokens per 100 changed lines, and the lead's own share -- of
every project, or of --project P.  A task is one message of the user's
and what it set off; `--tasks' lists each, newest first, a short one (a
go-ahead) with the one before it it goes on from: your own project's
only, which the herd knows you in -- another's tasks, and the user's
words in them, are not yours to read.

`reply' stores the answer and says so at once.  When your work on that
ask went rough -- many failed calls, denials, asks to one agent -- it
then says what made it rough and to `remember' a non-obvious gotcha
behind it; it looks three seconds at most, and says nothing more when
the work was smooth.

`start' and `stop' are for a lead: it runs agents in its own project
through the herd rather than by hand.  `start KIND' reuses an idle agent
it started whose branch is merged and worktree clean (fast-forwarding it,
keeping its context) before spawning a new one -- `--new' skips the
reuse.  A worktree is the default once another agent works in the
checkout; `--worktree [BRANCH]' forces one, `--no-worktree' runs in the
main checkout.  The herd caps how many a lead has up and refuses a
used-up kind, naming one with quota.  `stop NAME' kills an agent the
caller started -- not one owing an open or queued ask -- and removes its
worktree when merged and clean, else keeps it.

`remember', `recall' and `forget' are the herd's shared memory: curated
facts every agent of a project sees, whatever its CLI.  `remember TEXT'
writes one fact to your project's store (a worktree shares its main
checkout's), authored by you; `--type' is project (default), feedback,
reference or user, `--name' sets its slug.  Text that says again a fact
the store has is refused, naming it: run the same command again with
`--name NAME' to update that fact, or `--new' to keep both.  A `--name'
that exists is updated; the text it replaces, or that `forget' removes,
is kept in the store's .history/ (`recall' says what a fact was).

`search WORDS' finds what your project's past sessions said -- its
agents', yours, its worktrees' -- as a few short excerpts, each with its
session and turn; `search --session ID --at TURN' reads one on from
there.  Your own project only.  `recall' prints the project's
index, `recall NAME' that fact whole, or `recall QUERY' the facts most
relevant to QUERY in full, best first -- by meaning as well as words, so
a query in one language can find a fact written in another.  `forget
NAME' removes one.  `--user' is the store shared by every project (the user's
own preferences); `--project P' reaches another project's store from any
shell -- P a path, its leaf name (e.g. deploy-platform), or its slug.  Run
them from a plain shell too -- authored `user', for the project you are
in.  claude reads this memory through its own memory dir; agy and grok are
told to use these commands.

`promote propose' proposes moving stable, general facts out of memory and
into the project's instruction file (CLAUDE.md, or AGENTS.md where it links
to it), so every agent and machine sees them, versioned with the code.
Name the facts with `--fact' (repeatable), the file with `--file', and pipe
the exact diff on stdin.  The herd refuses a machine- or user-specific fact
(paths, credentials, personal preferences, the user store) and holds the
rest pending the user's approval on the page; on approval it asks the
project's lead to apply the diff by the project's branch/PR rules, and only
then does the fact leave memory.  The herd never edits the repo itself.

`promote propose --lint' proposes a check instead: a fact that guards
against real damage made into a rule run before every shell call, which
denies a call it matches with the fact's name and a hint.  The rule is
JSON on stdin -- {hint, check, catches, passes}, as bin/herd_lint.py
says -- and the herd holds it to its own examples: each of `catches' it
must deny, each of `passes' let through.  It is pending until the user
approves it on the page; then it is on for every agent of the fact's
store (--user: every agent), until the user turns it off.  The fact
stays a memory.  `lint check COMMAND' says which rule would deny
COMMAND here -- or, with --rule FILE, whether that candidate would.

Exit status: 0 answered, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 the answer comes to you
as a message instead (still open when --timeout ran out, or answered
while the sidecar was away), 4 failed or cancelled.  A wait that loses
the sidecar -- Emacs restarting -- waits for it to come back, five
minutes at most.

Env, set by ghostherd at spawn:
  GHOSTHERD_RPC       the sidecar's URL.  It carries a token: never
                      print it, and do not paste it anywhere.
  GHOSTHERD_RPC_FILE  where Emacs keeps the same URL, for a stale env
  GHOSTHERD_SESSION   your name; `user' when unset

`hook' is what claude's, grok's and agy's lifecycle hooks run: it tells
the herd what the agent is doing, which conversation it is on and, when
a turn ends, what it said.  `hooks install' wires it into each CLI's
settings; it does nothing in a CLI the herd did not start.

Python's standard library only, and nothing newer than 3.8: this runs
under whatever python3 the agent's shell finds.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import os
import sys

# `herd lint' runs before every shell call an agent makes: it answers
# from herd_lint.py before the rest of this file is imported (argparse,
# urllib... a tenth of the hook's time).
if __name__ == "__main__" and sys.argv[1:] == ["lint"]:
    sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    import herd_lint
    sys.exit(herd_lint.hook())

import argparse
import datetime
import decimal
import fnmatch
import hashlib
import json
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import tempfile
import threading
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

AWAIT_STEP = 50
DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 1800


class HerdError(Exception):
    pass


class Unreachable(HerdError):
    "The sidecar could not be reached, or refused the call -- not its answer."


# Emacs restarting restarts the sidecar, which keeps its asks: a wait
# that loses it waits for it to come back, this long at most.
RECONNECT_SECONDS = 300
RECONNECT_STEP = 1


def _env_url():
    return os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_RPC", "").strip()


def _file_url():
    path = os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_RPC_FILE", "").strip()
    if not path:
        return ""
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return f.read().strip()
    except OSError:
        return ""


def _where(url):
    "host:port of URL, for messages.  The path holds the token."
    parts = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)
    return parts.netloc or "the sidecar"


def _post(url, method, params, timeout):
    body = json.dumps(
        {"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": method, "params": params}
    ).encode("utf-8")
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        url, data=body, headers={"Content-Type": "application/json"}
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:
        return json.loads(resp.read().decode("utf-8"))


def rpc(method, params=None, timeout=15):
    """Call METHOD; return its result or raise HerdError.

    The env URL first, then the file's: an agent spawned before the
    sidecar's last restart holds a URL that is refused (401) or dead.
    """
    tried = []
    last = None
    for url in (_env_url(), _file_url()):
        if not url or url in tried:
            continue
        tried.append(url)
        try:
            data = _post(url, method, params or {}, timeout)
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
            last = "the sidecar at %s refused the call (HTTP %d)" % (_where(url), exc.code)
            continue
        except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError) as exc:
            reason = getattr(exc, "reason", exc)
            last = "cannot reach the sidecar at %s: %s" % (_where(url), reason)
            continue
        err = data.get("error")
        if err:
            raise HerdError(err.get("message") or "error")
        return data.get("result")
    if not tried:
        raise HerdError(
            "no sidecar URL: GHOSTHERD_RPC is unset (not an agent the herd "
            "started?) and so is GHOSTHERD_RPC_FILE"
        )
    raise Unreachable(last)


def me():
    return os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_SESSION", "").strip() or "user"


def text_arg(text):
    "TEXT, or stdin when it is `-' or missing."
    if text is not None and text != "-":
        return text
    if sys.stdin.isatty():
        raise HerdError("give the text as an argument, or pipe it in")
    return sys.stdin.read()


def say(msg):
    print("herd: " + msg, file=sys.stderr)


def show_answer(ask):
    if ask["status"] == "answered":
        if ask.get("auto"):
            what = "last message" if ask.get("auto_source") == "message" else "screen"
            say("%s stopped without answering; this is its %s" % (ask["to"], what))
        sys.stdout.write(ask.get("reply") or "")
        if not (ask.get("reply") or "").endswith("\n"):
            sys.stdout.write("\n")
        # How the taker's work went (the herd's counts, not a judgement):
        # beside the answer, never in it.
        if ask.get("trace"):
            sys.stdout.flush()
            say(ask["trace"])
        return 0
    say("ask %s %s: %s" % (ask["id"], ask["status"], ask.get("error") or ""))
    return 4


def wait_for(ask_id, to, timeout):
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
    seen = None
    lost = None  # since when the sidecar has been out of reach
    try:
        while True:
            left = deadline - time.monotonic()
            step = max(0, min(AWAIT_STEP, int(left)))
            try:
                ask = rpc("herd_await", {"id": ask_id, "timeout": step, "from": me()},
                          timeout=step + 15)
            except Unreachable as exc:
                now = time.monotonic()
                if lost is None:
                    lost = now
                    say("%s; waiting for it to come back" % exc)
                if now - lost >= RECONNECT_SECONDS or now >= deadline:
                    raise
                time.sleep(RECONNECT_STEP)
                continue
            if lost is not None:
                lost = None
                say("the sidecar is back")
            if ask["status"] in ("answered", "failed", "cancelled"):
                if ask.get("mailed"):
                    say("ask %s closed while the sidecar was away; its answer came to "
                        "you as a message" % ask_id)
                    return 3
                return show_answer(ask)
            now = (ask.get("status"), ask.get("taker_state"), ask.get("taker_reason"))
            if now != seen:
                seen = now
                state = ask.get("taker_state") or "?"
                reason = ask.get("taker_reason") or ""
                if ask["status"] == "queued":
                    say("%s is %s; the ask waits until it is free" % (to, state))
                else:
                    say("%s has it: %s%s" % (to, state, ("  " + reason) if reason else ""))
            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                break
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        try:
            rpc("herd_detach", {"id": ask_id})
        except Unreachable:
            pass
        say("stopped waiting; the answer will come to you as a message")
        return 130
    rpc("herd_detach", {"id": ask_id})
    say(
        "ask %s still open after %ds; the answer will come to you as a "
        "message (or: herd status %s)" % (ask_id, timeout, ask_id)
    )
    return 3


def cmd_ask(args):
    body = text_arg(args.text)
    params = {"to": args.to, "body": body, "from": me(), "wait": bool(args.wait)}
    if args.rounds is not None:
        params["rounds"] = args.rounds
    out = rpc("herd_ask", params)
    say("asked %s (ask %s)%s" % (
        out["to"], out["id"],
        ", round %d of %d" % (out["round"], out["of"]) if out.get("round") else ""))
    if not args.wait:
        print(out["id"])
        return 0
    return wait_for(out["id"], out["to"], args.timeout)


# How long `handoff' waits for the herd to start the lead of a project
# that has none, before it leaves the handoff to wait for it.
HANDOFF_START_WAIT = 60


def _project_arg(arg):
    """PROJECT as the sidecar takes it.  A path -- with a `/', or ~, `.' or
    `..' -- is made absolute here, against this shell's cwd, which is not
    the sidecar's; a name (unnoiac, .emacs.d, a slug) goes as given."""
    arg = (arg or "").strip()
    if "/" in arg or arg.startswith("~") or arg in (".", ".."):
        return os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(arg))
    return arg


def _await_taker(ask_id, seconds):
    """Wait up to SECONDS for the herd to start the lead a handoff goes to.
    The ask once it has its taker, or once it closed (refused); None while
    the lead is still starting."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + seconds
    while True:
        ask = rpc("herd_await", {"id": ask_id, "timeout": 0, "from": me()})
        if ask["status"] in ("answered", "failed", "cancelled") or ask.get("to"):
            return ask
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return None
        time.sleep(0.5)


def cmd_handoff(args):
    """Hand work to another project's lead: an ask of it, framed by the herd.
    A project with no lead gets one started there; this waits for it, and
    says so when it was refused."""
    body = text_arg(args.text)
    params = {"project": _project_arg(args.project), "body": body,
              "from": me(), "wait": bool(args.wait)}
    if args.rounds is not None:
        params["rounds"] = args.rounds
    out = rpc("herd_handoff", params)
    where = os.path.basename(out["project"].rstrip("/")) or out["project"]
    to = out["to"]
    rounds = ", round %d of %d" % (out["round"], out["of"]) if out.get("round") else ""
    if out.get("starting"):
        say("%s has no lead: the herd starts one there (handoff %s)" % (where, out["id"]))
        ask = _await_taker(out["id"], HANDOFF_START_WAIT)
        if ask is None:
            say("%s's lead is still starting; the handoff waits for it" % where)
        elif ask["status"] in ("answered", "failed", "cancelled"):
            return show_answer(ask)
        else:
            to = ask["to"]
            say("started %s, %s's lead" % (to, where))
    if to:
        say("handed off to %s, %s's lead (ask %s)%s" % (to, where, out["id"], rounds))
    if not args.wait:
        print(out["id"])
        return 0
    return wait_for(out["id"], to or "%s's lead" % where, args.timeout)


# How long `reply' looks, after the answer is in, for how the work went:
# the line is made just after the reply (the sidecar's `_trace_soon').
REPLY_NOTE_WAIT = 3.0


def _taker_note(ask_id, seconds):
    """What the herd tells the taker of ASK_ID when its work went rough, or
    None: the smooth case, no line within SECONDS, any error.  Looked for
    on a thread given SECONDS at most, whatever the sidecar does."""
    found = []

    def look():
        try:
            # From the taker: an onlooker, which never collects the answer.
            ask = rpc("herd_await", {"id": ask_id, "timeout": 0, "from": me()},
                      timeout=seconds)
            found.append(ask.get("taker_note"))
        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- no note, never a failed reply
            pass

    t = threading.Thread(target=look, daemon=True)
    t.start()
    t.join(seconds)
    note = found[0] if found else None
    return note if isinstance(note, str) and note.strip() else None


def cmd_reply(args):
    out = rpc(
        "herd_reply", {"id": args.id, "body": text_arg(args.text), "from": me()}
    )
    say("answered ask %s" % out["id"])
    # Only an agent hears how its work went: the answer is in and on its
    # way already; this only holds the exit, REPLY_NOTE_WAIT at most.
    if os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_SESSION", "").strip():
        sys.stderr.flush()
        note = _taker_note(out["id"], REPLY_NOTE_WAIT)
        for line in (note or "").splitlines():
            say(line)
    return 0


def cmd_status(args):
    print(json.dumps(rpc("herd_await", {"id": args.id, "timeout": 0, "from": me()}),
                     indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    return 0


def cmd_cancel(args):
    out = rpc("herd_cancel", {"id": args.id})
    say("ask %s %s" % (out["id"], out["status"]))
    return 0


def cmd_list(_args):
    print(json.dumps(rpc("herd_list"), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    return 0


def cmd_asks(_args):
    print(json.dumps(rpc("herd_asks"), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))


def _tokens(n):
    "N as the page writes it: 12M, 1.3M, 340k, 999 -- halves up; None as a dash."
    if n is None:
        return "—"
    if n >= 1000000:
        if not n % 1000000:
            return "%dM" % (n // 1000000)
        v = decimal.Decimal(n / 1000000.0).quantize(decimal.Decimal("0.1"), decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP).normalize()
        return "%sM" % format(v, "f")
    return "%dk" % int(n / 1000.0 + 0.5) if n >= 1000 else str(n)


def cmd_cost(args):
    """Lead mode against direct mode: what a task costs, over the last
    --days local days; --tasks lists each task."""
    out = rpc("herd_costs", {"days": args.days, "project": args.project or "", "tasks": args.tasks, "from": me()})
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    c = out["compare"]
    lead, direct = c["lead"], c["direct"]
    print("Tasks in the last %d days (since %s)%s, in weighted tokens:\n" % (
        c["days"], c["since"], " in " + args.project if args.project else ""))
    rows = (
        ("tasks", str(lead["tasks"]), str(direct["tasks"])),
        ("median per task", _tokens(lead["median"]), _tokens(direct["median"])),
        # A go-ahead is a task of its own: the tasks that changed code apart.
        ("median per coded task", _tokens(lead.get("medianCoded")), _tokens(direct.get("medianCoded"))),
        ("total", _tokens(lead["total"]), _tokens(direct["total"])),
        ("per 100 lines", _tokens(lead["per100"]), _tokens(direct["per100"])),
        ("lines changed", "%d in %d" % (lead["lines"], lead["coded"]), "%d in %d" % (direct["lines"], direct["coded"])),
        ("of them merged", str(lead.get("merged", 0)), str(direct.get("merged", 0))),
        ("no code", str(lead["noCode"]), str(direct["noCode"])),
        ("not read yet", str(lead.get("pending", 0)), str(direct.get("pending", 0))),
        ("not readable", str(lead["unknown"]), str(direct["unknown"])),
        ("lead's own share", "—" if lead["own"] is None else "%d%%" % lead["own"], "—"),
    )
    print("%-21s %14s %14s" % ("", "lead mode", "direct"))
    for name, a, b in rows:
        print("%-21s %14s %14s" % (name, a, b))
    for t in out.get("tasks") or []:
        when = datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(t["at"]).strftime("%m-%d %H:%M") if t.get("at") else "?"
        made = {"no": "no code", "unknown": "code not readable", "pending": "code not read yet"}.get(
            t["code"], "%d lines (%d of %d commits merged)" % (t["lines"], t.get("merged", 0), t.get("commits", 0)))
        print("\n%s  %-6s %s  %s (own %s, workers %s, sub-agents %s)  %s\n  %s" % (
            when, t["mode"], t["agent"], _tokens(t["total"]), _tokens(t["own"]), _tokens(t["workers"]),
            # A short prompt -- a go-ahead -- with the one it goes on from.
            _tokens(t["subs"]), made, t["prompt"][:100] + (" ← " + t["context"] if t.get("context") else "")))
    if out.get("withheld"):
        print("\n(%d more task%s: an agent is shown its own project's tasks only -- the rest are in the "
              "numbers above, and on the herd page)" % (out["withheld"], "" if out["withheld"] == 1 else "s"))
    return 0


def _cwd_project():
    "The git checkout of the shell's cwd, a project hint for a plain user."
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"],
                             stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                             timeout=5)
        return out.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace").strip() if out.returncode == 0 else ""
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return ""


def _mem_params(args):
    "Common memory params: who asks and, as a fallback, the project in cwd."
    params = {"from": me(), "project": _cwd_project()}
    if getattr(args, "user", False):
        params["user"] = True
    # An explicit --project (a path, leaf name, or slug) overrides the session
    # and the cwd, so the user can reach any project's memory from any shell.
    project = getattr(args, "project", None)
    if project:
        params["project"] = project
        params["project_given"] = True
    return params


def cmd_remember(args):
    text = text_arg(args.text)
    if not text.strip():
        raise HerdError("nothing to remember")
    params = _mem_params(args)
    params["text"] = text
    if args.type:
        params["type"] = args.type
    if args.name:
        params["name"] = args.name
    if args.new:
        params["new"] = True
    out = rpc("herd_remember", params)
    where = "user memory" if out["store"] == "user" else "this project"
    status = out.get("status") or "new"
    if status == "unchanged":
        say("already remembered as `%s' (%s, %s): nothing changed" % (out["name"], out["type"], where))
    elif status == "updated":
        say("updated `%s' (%s, %s); its earlier text is kept in its history"
            % (out["name"], out["type"], where))
    elif status == "renamed":
        say("remembered as `%s' (%s, %s): its usual name is another fact's"
            % (out["name"], out["type"], where))
    else:
        say("remembered `%s' (%s, %s)" % (out["name"], out["type"], where))
    if out.get("checked") == "unchecked":
        say("(not checked against the facts there: the sidecar's embedder is not up yet)")
    return 0


def cmd_recall(args):
    params = _mem_params(args)
    query = " ".join(args.query or []).strip()
    if query:
        params["query"] = query
    out = rpc("herd_recall", params)
    sys.stdout.write((out.get("text") or out.get("index") or "").rstrip() + "\n")
    return 0


def cmd_search(args):
    params = {"from": me()}
    query = " ".join(args.query or []).strip()
    if args.session:
        params["session"] = args.session
        params["at"] = args.at
    elif query:
        params["query"] = query
    else:
        raise HerdError("search for what?  herd search WORDS, or --session ID")
    out = rpc("herd_search", params, timeout=30)
    sys.stdout.write((out.get("text") or "").rstrip() + "\n")
    return 0


def cmd_forget(args):
    params = _mem_params(args)
    params["name"] = args.name
    out = rpc("herd_forget", params)
    say(("forgot `%s'" % out["name"]) if out["removed"]
        else ("no fact named `%s'" % out["name"]))
    return 0 if out["removed"] else 1


def cmd_promote(args):
    """Propose promoting stable, general facts into the project's instruction
    file.  The exact diff comes on stdin.  The herd holds it pending the user's
    approval on the page; nothing is written to the repo here.  With --lint,
    a check made of one fact instead: the rule, JSON, on stdin.  With
    --every-project, one fact moved to the user store."""
    if args.every_project:
        return _propose_share(args)
    if args.lint:
        return _propose_lint(args)
    if not args.file:
        raise HerdError("--file is required (the instruction file, e.g. CLAUDE.md)")
    if not args.fact:
        raise HerdError("name at least one fact with --fact NAME (repeatable)")
    diff = text_arg("-")
    if not diff.strip():
        raise HerdError("pipe the exact diff in on stdin")
    params = _mem_params(args)
    params.update(facts=args.fact, file=args.file, diff=diff)
    out = rpc("herd_promote_propose", params)
    say("proposed promoting %s into %s (pending the user's approval)"
        % (", ".join(out["facts"]), out["file"]))
    return 0


def _propose_share(args):
    """`promote propose --every-project': one fact of this project moved to the
    user store, so every project has it -- its check and its counts too --
    once the user approves.  Nothing on stdin."""
    if args.file or args.lint or args.user:
        raise HerdError("--every-project moves a project fact to the user store: no --file, --lint or --user")
    if not args.fact or len(args.fact) != 1:
        raise HerdError("move one fact at a time: name it with --fact NAME, once")
    params = _mem_params(args)
    params.update(facts=args.fact, share=True)
    out = rpc("herd_promote_propose", params, timeout=30)
    say("proposed making %s every project's (pending the user's approval)%s"
        % (out["facts"][0], " -- the same one was already waiting" if out.get("duplicate") else ""))
    return 0


def _propose_lint(args):
    "`promote propose --lint': one fact's check, pending the user's approval."
    if args.file:
        raise HerdError("--lint proposes a check, not a change to --file")
    if not args.fact or len(args.fact) != 1:
        raise HerdError("a check is one fact's: name it with --fact NAME, once")
    text = text_arg("-")
    try:
        rule = json.loads(text)
    except ValueError as exc:
        raise HerdError("the rule on stdin is not JSON: %s" % exc)
    if not isinstance(rule, dict):
        raise HerdError("the rule on stdin is a JSON object: {hint, check, catches, passes}")
    params = _mem_params(args)
    params.update(facts=args.fact, lint=dict(rule, fact=args.fact[0]))
    out = rpc("herd_promote_propose", params, timeout=30)
    say("proposed a check for %s (pending the user's approval)%s"
        % (out["facts"][0], " -- the same one was already waiting" if out.get("duplicate") else ""))
    return 0


def _lint_module():
    sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    import herd_lint
    return herd_lint


def cmd_lint(args):
    """`lint check COMMAND': the rule that would deny COMMAND here, or that
    none would.  Exit 0 when it would run, 3 when a rule denies it."""
    lint = _lint_module()
    command = text_arg(args.text)
    rule = None
    if args.rule:
        try:
            with open(args.rule, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                rule = json.load(f)
        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
            raise HerdError("--rule %s: %s" % (args.rule, exc))
        if not isinstance(rule, dict):
            raise HerdError("--rule %s: not a JSON object" % args.rule)
        rule.setdefault("fact", "candidate")
    try:
        hit = lint.check(command, cwd=args.cwd, rule=rule)
    except ValueError as exc:
        raise HerdError(str(exc))
    if hit is None:
        print("runs: no check denies it")
        return 0
    key, r = hit
    print("denied by the check for `%s' (%s): %s" % (r.fact, key, r.hint))
    return 3


def cmd_memory(args):
    """Move the existing claude memories into the store, or put them back.
    Backs each original up first and is reversible; prints a report."""
    params = {}
    if args.project:
        params["projects"] = args.project
    if args.action == "unmigrate":
        out = rpc("memory_unmigrate", params, timeout=120)
    else:
        if args.user_name:
            params["user_names"] = args.user_name
        params["dry_run"] = args.action == "plan"
        out = rpc("memory_migrate", params, timeout=120)
    print(json.dumps(out, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    if args.action in ("migrate",) and not (out.get("verify") or {}).get("ok", True):
        say("migration done but verify found problems; see the report")
        return 1
    return 0


def cmd_relay(args):
    """Hand an agent's work to a fresh agent on another CLI, through the same
    path the herd page and Telegram use.  Prints what the herd did, or why it
    refused."""
    kind = (args.kind or "").strip()
    reason = text_arg(args.reason) if args.reason else ""
    out = rpc("herd_relay", {"target": args.target, "kind": kind,
                             "reason": reason, "by": me()})
    cid = out.get("id")
    if not cid:
        print(out.get("text") or "relay: no reply from the herd")
        return 1
    # It runs in Emacs on the next herd tick; wait for its word.
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 20
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        r = rpc("herd_command_reply", {"id": cid})
        status, text = r.get("status"), r.get("text")
        if status == "done" and text is not None:
            print(text)
            return 0 if str(text).startswith("relaying ") else 1
        if status == "gone":
            print("relay: the request was dropped before it ran")
            return 1
        time.sleep(0.4)
    print("relay: timed out waiting for the herd to act")
    return 1


def _parse_since(s):
    """WHEN as epoch seconds: `3d'/`2h'/`90m'/`30s' back, `today'/`yesterday',
    or an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD, optionally with a time).  None when S is empty."""
    s = (s or "").strip()
    if not s:
        return None
    m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d+)\s*([dhms])", s, re.I)
    if m:
        unit = {"d": 86400, "h": 3600, "m": 60, "s": 1}[m.group(2).lower()]
        return time.time() - int(m.group(1)) * unit
    midnight = datetime.datetime.now().replace(hour=0, minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0)
    if s.lower() == "today":
        return midnight.timestamp()
    if s.lower() == "yesterday":
        return (midnight - datetime.timedelta(days=1)).timestamp()
    for fmt in ("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S", "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S",
                "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M", "%Y-%m-%d"):
        try:
            return datetime.datetime.strptime(s, fmt).timestamp()
        except ValueError:
            pass
    raise HerdError("--since: use 3d/2h/90m, today, yesterday, or YYYY-MM-DD")


def _await_command(out, label, ok_prefixes):
    """Poll a queued command (start/stop) to its reply, print it, and return an
    exit code: 0 when the reply begins with one of OK_PREFIXES, else 1."""
    cid = out.get("id")
    if not cid:
        text = out.get("text")
        print(text if text else "herd: %s: no reply from the herd" % label,
              file=sys.stderr if not text else sys.stdout)
        return 1
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 30
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        r = rpc("herd_command_reply", {"id": cid})
        status, text = r.get("status"), r.get("text")
        if status == "done" and text is not None:
            print(text)
            return 0 if str(text).startswith(tuple(ok_prefixes)) else 1
        if status == "gone":
            say("%s: the request was dropped before it ran" % label)
            return 1
        time.sleep(0.4)
    say("%s: timed out waiting for the herd (it may be busy or just restarted; try again)" % label)
    return 1


def cmd_start(args):
    """Start, or reuse, an agent in your project.  Only a lead may, for its own
    project.  Prints the agent's name (and its worktree), or why it was
    refused."""
    if args.no_worktree:
        worktree, branch = "no", ""
    elif args.worktree is True:
        worktree, branch = "yes", ""
    elif isinstance(args.worktree, str):
        worktree, branch = "yes", args.worktree
    else:
        worktree, branch = "auto", ""
    out = rpc("herd_start", {
        "by": me(), "kind": (args.kind or "").strip(),
        "worktree": worktree, "branch": branch,
        "name": (args.name or "").strip(),
        "notes": text_arg(args.notes) if args.notes else "",
        "new": bool(args.new),
    })
    return _await_command(out, "start", ("started ", "reused "))


def cmd_stop(args):
    """Stop an agent you started.  Refused for one you did not start, or one
    holding an open or queued ask."""
    out = rpc("herd_stop", {"by": me(), "name": (args.name or "").strip()})
    return _await_command(out, "stop", ("stopped ",))


def cmd_screens(args):
    """Print saved agent screens from the herd log -- time, agent, reason and
    the screen -- filtered by --agent, --since and --why.  Read-only; it
    round-trips through Emacs on a herd tick, where the log lives, the same
    path `relay' uses."""
    since = _parse_since(args.since)
    out = rpc("herd_screens", {"agent": (args.agent or "").strip(),
                               "since": since, "why": (args.why or "").strip(),
                               "by": me()})
    cid = out.get("id")
    if not cid:
        say("no reply from the herd")
        return 1
    deadline = time.monotonic() + 20
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        r = rpc("herd_command_reply", {"id": cid})
        status, text = r.get("status"), r.get("text")
        if status == "done" and text is not None:
            print(text)
            return 0
        if status == "gone":
            say("the request was dropped before it ran")
            return 1
        time.sleep(0.4)
    # The query rides a herd tick; if Emacs is mid-reconnect after a sidecar
    # restart it may not have ticked yet.  A second call lands normally.
    say("timed out waiting for the herd (it may be busy or just restarted; try again)")
    return 1


# ---- Hooks ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One command for every CLI's lifecycle hooks.  `herd hook [EVENT]' reads
# the hook's JSON on stdin and tells the sidecar what the agent is doing,
# which conversation it is on, and -- when a turn ends -- what it said.
#
# A hook must never get in its CLI's way: this always exits 0, prints
# nothing a CLI would act on (agy wants `{}', so it gets exactly that),
# and does nothing at all in a CLI the herd did not start.

LAST_MAX = 32768
TAIL_BYTES = 512 * 1024
# A turn fires `working' often (agy: before every model call); the herd
# needs it again only before its report expires (120s).
WORKING_EVERY = 30
# Events whose hooks agy runs: it wants a JSON object back from each.
AGY_EVENTS = ("PreInvocation", "PostInvocation")


def _payload():
    if sys.stdin.isatty():
        return {}
    raw = sys.stdin.read()
    try:
        data = json.loads(raw) if raw.strip() else {}
    except ValueError:
        return {}
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}


def _cli(p):
    "Which CLI sent payload P, from the keys only it uses."
    if "conversationId" in p:
        return "agy"
    if "sessionId" in p or "hookEventName" in p:
        return "grok"
    if "session_id" in p:
        return "claude"
    return ""


def _tail(path):
    "PATH's last lines, newest first; [] when it cannot be read."
    try:
        with open(path, "rb") as f:
            f.seek(0, 2)
            size = f.tell()
            f.seek(max(0, size - TAIL_BYTES))
            data = f.read()
    except OSError:
        return []
    lines = data.decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines()
    if size > TAIL_BYTES:
        lines = lines[1:]  # cut mid-line
    return [l for l in reversed(lines) if l.strip()]


def _records(path):
    for line in _tail(path):
        try:
            o = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if isinstance(o, dict):
            yield o


def claude_last(path):
    """The answer that ended claude's turn, from its transcript, or None.

    Walks back from the end.  A prompt of the user's met before any
    answer means this turn's answer is not there, and what lies beyond
    it is an older turn's -- the wrong answer, so None instead.  An
    answer is every text block of the last assistant message: claude
    writes one record per block.
    """
    found = None
    parts = []
    for o in _records(path):
        if o.get("isSidechain"):
            continue
        msg = o.get("message") if isinstance(o.get("message"), dict) else {}
        content = msg.get("content")
        if o.get("type") == "assistant":
            texts = [b.get("text", "") for b in content or []
                     if isinstance(b, dict) and b.get("type") == "text"] \
                if isinstance(content, list) else []
            text = "\n".join(t for t in texts if t.strip())
            if found is None:
                if text:
                    found = msg.get("id") or ""
                    parts.append(text)
            elif (msg.get("id") or "") == found:
                if text:
                    parts.append(text)
            else:
                break
        elif o.get("type") == "user" and not o.get("isMeta"):
            prompt = (isinstance(content, str) and content.strip()) or (
                isinstance(content, list)
                and any(isinstance(b, dict) and b.get("type") == "text" for b in content)
            )
            if prompt:
                break
            if found is not None:
                break
    return "\n\n".join(reversed(parts)) or None


def agy_last(path):
    "The answer that ended agy's turn, from its transcript, or None."
    for o in _records(path):
        if o.get("type") == "USER_INPUT":
            return None
        if (o.get("source") == "MODEL" and o.get("type") == "PLANNER_RESPONSE"
                and o.get("content") and not o.get("tool_calls")):
            return o["content"]
    return None


def grok_history(path):
    """The conversation grok keeps beside PATH, or PATH: its hooks name
    updates.jsonl, its screen's stream of updates, not the conversation."""
    if path and os.path.basename(path) != "chat_history.jsonl":
        history = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(path), "chat_history.jsonl")
        if os.path.isfile(history):
            return history
    return path


def hook_report(p, event=None):
    """What hook payload P says about the agent.

    A dict of state, reason, last (its answer, when a turn ended), cli,
    conversation and transcript; the falsy ones are not news.
    """
    cli = _cli(p)
    event = p.get("hook_event_name") or event or ""
    transcript = p.get("transcript_path") or p.get("transcriptPath") or ""
    if cli == "grok":
        transcript = grok_history(transcript)
    out = {
        "cli": cli,
        "conversation": p.get("session_id") or p.get("sessionId") or p.get("conversationId") or "",
        "transcript": transcript,
        "state": None,
        "reason": None,
        "last": None,
    }
    if event in ("UserPromptSubmit", "PreInvocation"):
        out["state"] = "working"
    elif event == "Notification":
        kind = p.get("notification_type") or p.get("notificationType") or ""
        msg = (p.get("message") or "").strip()
        if kind == "permission_prompt" or (not kind and re.search(r"permission|approv", msg, re.I)):
            out["state"], out["reason"] = "blocked", msg or "waiting for permission"
    elif event == "Stop":
        # grok fires one more Stop as the session closes: not a turn.
        if cli == "grok" and p.get("reason") not in (None, "end_turn"):
            return out
        if cli == "agy" and p.get("terminationReason") == "error":
            out["state"], out["reason"] = "done", "stopped: " + (p.get("error") or "error")
        else:
            out["state"], out["reason"] = "done", "finished its turn"
        last = p.get("lastAssistantMessage") or p.get("last_assistant_message")
        if not last and transcript:
            last = (agy_last if cli == "agy" else claude_last)(transcript)
        out["last"] = last[:LAST_MAX] if last else None
    elif event == "StopFailure":
        out["state"], out["reason"] = "done", "stopped: " + (p.get("error") or "error")
    elif event == "StopCancelled":
        out["state"] = "auto"  # interrupted: the screen knows better now
    return out


# What a CLI may run its hook through: shells and wrappers, not the CLI.
_RUNNERS = {"sh", "bash", "zsh", "dash", "ksh", "fish", "tcsh", "csh",
            "env", "timeout", "nice", "nohup"}


def _lineage():
    """(PID, ANCESTORS): the process of the CLI that ran this hook -- the
    nearest one above it that is not a shell or a wrapper -- and the
    processes above that, nearest first.  The herd tells the agent's own
    CLI from one the agent runs (a probe, under the agent's name) by them.
    (None, []) when `ps' cannot say: the herd then goes by the kind alone."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-A", "-o", "pid=,ppid=,comm="],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=3).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None, []
    procs = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        parts = line.split(None, 2)
        if len(parts) >= 2 and parts[0].isdigit() and parts[1].isdigit():
            name = os.path.basename(parts[2].strip()).lstrip("-") if len(parts) > 2 else ""
            procs[int(parts[0])] = (int(parts[1]), name)
    pid, seen = os.getppid(), set()
    while pid in procs and procs[pid][1] in _RUNNERS and pid not in seen:
        seen.add(pid)
        pid = procs[pid][0]
    if pid not in procs or pid <= 1:
        return None, []
    ancestors, up = [], procs[pid][0]
    while up in procs and up > 1 and up not in seen:
        seen.add(up)
        ancestors.append(up)
        up = procs[up][0]
    return pid, ancestors


def _headless(cli):
    """True when CLI runs one prompt and exits (`claude -p', the Agent SDK):
    a herd agent never does.  claude says so in its children's environment
    -- CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT `sdk-cli', `sdk-ts', ... against `cli' --
    setting it itself, over whatever it inherited (measured on 2.1.308)."""
    return cli == "claude" and os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT", "").startswith("sdk")


def _stamp_file(session):
    key = hashlib.sha1(session.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()[:16]
    return os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), "ghostherd-hook-%s.json" % key)


def _repeat(session, news):
    "True when NEWS only repeats a `working' sent moments ago."
    if news.get("state") != "working" or news.get("last"):
        return False
    try:
        with open(_stamp_file(session), encoding="utf-8") as f:
            was = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False
    return (was.get("state") == "working"
            and was.get("conversation") == news.get("conversation")
            and time.time() - float(was.get("at") or 0) < WORKING_EVERY)


def _remember(session, news):
    try:
        with open(_stamp_file(session), "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
            json.dump({"state": news.get("state"), "conversation": news.get("conversation"),
                       "at": time.time()}, f)
    except OSError:
        pass


def cmd_hook(args):
    p = _payload()
    agy = _cli(p) == "agy" or args.event in AGY_EVENTS
    session = os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_SESSION", "").strip()
    try:
        if session:
            news = {k: v for k, v in hook_report(p, args.event).items() if v}
            if (news.get("state") or news.get("conversation")) and not _repeat(session, news):
                # Which CLI this is: a CLI the agent runs inherits its name,
                # and the herd must not take it for the agent.
                pid, ancestors = _lineage()
                extra = {"headless": True} if _headless(news.get("cli")) else {}
                out = rpc("herd_report", dict(news, session=session, pid=pid,
                                              ancestors=ancestors, **extra), timeout=3)
                if not (out or {}).get("ignored"):
                    _remember(session, news)
    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- a hook must never fail its CLI
        say("hook: %s" % exc)
    if agy:
        print("{}")
    return 0


# ---- The guard of an agy agent --------------------------------------------
#
# A guarded agy runs with --dangerously-skip-permissions and this as its
# PreToolUse hook: the only gate, deciding here, from the policy the herd
# wrote into the agent's guard directory (bin/herd_guard.py).  A denial is
# told to the herd, for the card and the log, and one the user may approve
# names its request.  The answer never waits on that: no sidecar, or a slow
# one, changes nothing but the telling.


def _guard_module():
    sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
    import herd_guard
    return herd_guard


GUARD_REPORT_TIMEOUT = 2


def _guard_lint(guard_dir, payload):
    """The herd's checks on a guarded agy's shell call (bin/herd_lint.py):
    their deny, or None.  Asked before the guard, so a check denies
    whatever the guard would say, and an approval the user gave once is not
    spent on a call that cannot run; a check never allows.  Their failure
    is no decision: the guard decides, as ever."""
    try:
        lint = _lint_module()
        with open(os.path.join(guard_dir, "policy.json"), encoding="utf-8") as f:
            workspace = json.load(f).get("workspace")
        hit = lint.decide(payload, cwd=workspace)
        if hit is None:
            return None
        cli, key, rule, command = hit
        lint.report(cli, key, rule, command, timeout=GUARD_REPORT_TIMEOUT)
        return lint.answer(cli, rule)
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- fail open: the guard still decides
        return None


def cmd_guard(args):
    "agy's PreToolUse hook for a guarded agent: allow or deny, never anything else."
    verdict = call = None
    try:
        guard = _guard_module()
        payload = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "{}")
        denied = _guard_lint(args.dir, payload)
        if denied is not None:
            print(json.dumps(denied, ensure_ascii=False))
            return 0
        answer, verdict, call = guard.judge(args.dir, payload)
    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- the guard's failure is a denial
        answer = {"decision": "deny",
                  "reason": "The herd's guard could not check this call (%s); tell the user." % exc}
    if verdict is not None and (verdict.decision == "deny" or verdict.kind == "approved"):
        try:
            if verdict.kind == "approved":
                rpc("herd_guard_used", {"id": verdict.rule.split(":", 1)[1]},
                    timeout=GUARD_REPORT_TIMEOUT)
            else:
                out = rpc("herd_guard_denied", {
                    "session": os.environ.get("GHOSTHERD_SESSION") or "",
                    "guard_dir": os.path.realpath(args.dir),
                    "tool": str((call or {}).get("name") or ""),
                    "summary": guard.summary(call),
                    "reason": verdict.reason, "rule": verdict.rule, "kind": verdict.kind,
                    "approvable": verdict.approvable, "fp": guard.fingerprint(call),
                    "call": json.dumps(call, ensure_ascii=False)[:4000],
                }, timeout=GUARD_REPORT_TIMEOUT)
                if verdict.approvable and isinstance(out, dict) and out.get("status") == "declined":
                    answer["reason"] = ("The user kept this exact call denied: don't retry it; say "
                                        "what you needed instead. [request %s]" % out["id"])
                elif verdict.approvable and isinstance(out, dict) and out.get("id"):
                    answer["reason"] = answer.get("reason", "") + " [request %s]" % out["id"]
        except (HerdError, OSError, ValueError):
            pass
    print(json.dumps(answer, ensure_ascii=False))
    return 0


# A URL's user part: `http://user:password@proxy', `https://TOKEN@host'.
_URL_CREDENTIAL = re.compile(r"://[^/\s@]+@")


def allowed_env(environ, allow):
    """ENVIRON with only the names ALLOW lets through -- exact names, or
    globs (LC_*, XDG_*) -- and none whose value carries a credential in a
    URL (a proxy with a password): what is not there cannot leak."""
    return {k: v for k, v in environ.items()
            if any(fnmatch.fnmatchcase(k, pat) for pat in allow) and not _URL_CREDENTIAL.search(v)}


def cmd_scrub_exec(args):
    """Run CMD with only the --allow names in the environment it really has
    -- or, without --allow, with the names --scrub matches dropped and the
    --keep ones kept -- replacing this process with it (one pid, the CLI's)."""
    if args.allow:
        env = allowed_env(os.environ, args.allow)
    else:
        pats = [re.compile(p) for p in args.scrub or []]
        keep = set(args.keep or [])
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k in keep or not any(p.search(k) for p in pats)}
    cmd = [c for c in (args.cmd or []) if c != "--"]
    if not cmd:
        raise HerdError("scrub-exec: give the command after --")
    try:
        os.execvpe(cmd[0], cmd, env)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise HerdError("scrub-exec: %s: %s" % (cmd[0], exc))


# ---- Installing the hooks ------------------------------------------------
#
# claude reads ~/.claude/settings.json, and grok reads the same file
# unless told not to, with the same event names -- one entry serves
# both.  agy reads ~/.gemini/config/hooks.json, as named hook specs.
# Each command does nothing outside the herd, so it is safe in settings
# every session of the CLI reads.
#
# The checks (`herd lint') are claude's and grok's PreToolUse on a shell
# call: matcher Bash, which grok reads as its run_terminal_command too.
# agy's are its guard's (`herd guard' asks them first): a second
# PreToolUse in agy's own hooks.json would sit beside the guard's, and
# how agy weighs two answers is not measured -- a `{}' after the guard's
# deny must not be what lets a call through.

MARK = '"$GHOSTHERD_HERD" hook'
LINT_MARK = '"$GHOSTHERD_HERD" lint'
CLAUDE_EVENTS = ("SessionStart", "UserPromptSubmit", "Notification", "Stop")
LINT_EVENT, LINT_MATCHER = "PreToolUse", "Bash"
CLAUDE_HOOKS = CLAUDE_EVENTS + (LINT_EVENT,)
AGY_HOOKS = ("PreInvocation", "Stop")


def claude_settings():
    return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".claude", "settings.json")


def agy_hooks_file():
    return os.path.join(os.path.expanduser("~"), ".gemini", "config", "hooks.json")


def _claude_command():
    return '[ -z "$GHOSTHERD_HERD" ] || ' + MARK


def _lint_command():
    return '[ -z "$GHOSTHERD_HERD" ] || ' + LINT_MARK


def _claude_entry(event):
    "The settings entry for EVENT: the checks' on a shell call, else the report."
    if event == LINT_EVENT:
        return {"matcher": LINT_MATCHER,
                "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": _lint_command(), "timeout": 5}]}
    return {"hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": _claude_command(), "timeout": 10}]}


def _agy_command(event):
    return ('if [ -n "$GHOSTHERD_HERD" ]; then %s %s; else echo \'{}\'; fi'
            % (MARK, event))


def _ours(handler):
    command = str(handler.get("command") or "") if isinstance(handler, dict) else ""
    return MARK in command or LINT_MARK in command


def _load(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            data = json.load(f)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {}
    except ValueError as exc:
        raise HerdError("%s is not valid JSON (%s); fix it first" % (path, exc))
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        raise HerdError("%s is not a JSON object" % path)
    return data


def _save(path, data, dry_run, preview):
    """Write DATA to PATH, backing the old file up; with DRY_RUN, show
    PREVIEW instead -- only the entries that change, never the rest of
    a settings file, which may hold keys."""
    if dry_run:
        print(json.dumps(preview, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
        return
    text = json.dumps(data, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    if os.path.exists(path):
        backup = "%s.ghostherd-%s.bak" % (path, time.strftime("%Y%m%d%H%M%S"))
        shutil.copy2(path, backup)
        say("backed up %s" % backup)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path + ".ghostherd-tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w", encoding="utf-8") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, path)
    say("wrote %s" % path)


def claude_installed(data):
    hooks = data.get("hooks") if isinstance(data.get("hooks"), dict) else {}
    return [ev for ev in CLAUDE_HOOKS
            if any(_ours(h) for g in hooks.get(ev) or [] if isinstance(g, dict)
                   for h in g.get("hooks") or [])]


def agy_installed(data):
    spec = data.get("ghostherd") if isinstance(data.get("ghostherd"), dict) else {}
    return [ev for ev in AGY_HOOKS if any(_ours(h) for h in spec.get(ev) or [])]


def install_claude(data):
    hooks = data.setdefault("hooks", {})
    have = claude_installed(data)
    for ev in CLAUDE_HOOKS:
        if ev not in have:
            hooks.setdefault(ev, []).append(_claude_entry(ev))
    return [ev for ev in CLAUDE_HOOKS if ev not in have]


def uninstall_claude(data):
    hooks = data.get("hooks") if isinstance(data.get("hooks"), dict) else {}
    removed = []
    for ev in list(hooks):
        groups = hooks[ev] if isinstance(hooks[ev], list) else []
        kept = []
        for g in groups:
            if isinstance(g, dict) and isinstance(g.get("hooks"), list):
                left = [h for h in g["hooks"] if not _ours(h)]
                if len(left) != len(g["hooks"]):
                    removed.append(ev)
                if left:
                    kept.append(dict(g, hooks=left))
            else:
                kept.append(g)
        if kept:
            hooks[ev] = kept
        else:
            del hooks[ev]
    if "hooks" in data and not data["hooks"]:
        del data["hooks"]
    return removed


def install_agy(data):
    have = agy_installed(data)
    data["ghostherd"] = {
        ev: [{"type": "command", "command": _agy_command(ev), "timeout": 10}]
        for ev in AGY_HOOKS
    }
    return [ev for ev in AGY_HOOKS if ev not in have]


def cmd_hooks(args):
    targets = (
        ("claude/grok", claude_settings(), claude_installed, install_claude, uninstall_claude,
         lambda evs: {"hooks": {ev: [_claude_entry(ev)] for ev in evs}}),
        ("agy", agy_hooks_file(), agy_installed, install_agy,
         lambda d: list(d.pop("ghostherd", {}) or {}),
         lambda evs: {"ghostherd": {ev: [{"type": "command", "command": _agy_command(ev),
                                          "timeout": 10}] for ev in evs}}),
    )
    for name, path, installed, install, uninstall, preview in targets:
        data = _load(path)
        if args.action == "status":
            have = installed(data)
            print("%-12s %s: %s" % (name, path, ", ".join(have) if have else "not installed"))
            continue
        changed = install(data) if args.action == "install" else uninstall(data)
        if changed:
            verb = {"install": "add", "uninstall": "remove"}[args.action]
            print("%-12s %s %s: %s" % (
                name, ("would " + verb + " in") if args.dry_run else (verb + "ed in"),
                path, ", ".join(changed)))
            _save(path, data, args.dry_run, preview(changed))
        else:
            print("%-12s %s: nothing to do" % (name, path))
    return 0


# ---- Every hook each CLI runs ----------------------------------------------
#
# `herd hooks list' reads every place claude, grok and agy look for hooks
# -- user settings, a project's, plugins, grok's own directory and its
# Claude/Cursor compatibility -- and lists each handler with the file and
# line it is on, and which CLIs run it.  Read-only.

def _read(path):
    try:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            return f.read()
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError):
        return None


def _line(text, needle, start=0):
    "1-based line of NEEDLE in TEXT at or after START, or None."
    i = text.find(needle, max(0, start))
    return None if i < 0 else text.count("\n", 0, i) + 1


def _toml(text):
    try:
        import tomllib  # 3.11+
    except ImportError:
        return None
    try:
        return tomllib.loads(text)
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
        return None


def _grok_compat(vendor):
    "Whether grok reads VENDOR's hooks (on unless its config says not)."
    data = _toml(_read(os.path.expanduser("~/.grok/config.toml")) or "") or {}
    cell = ((data.get("compat") or {}).get(vendor) or {}) if isinstance(data, dict) else {}
    return cell.get("hooks", True) is not False


def _entries(path, text, events, readers, scope, source, enabled=True):
    """Handlers in EVENTS, a {event: [group or handler]} map from PATH.

    A group is {matcher, hooks: [handler]}; a bare handler (agy's flat
    events, Cursor's) stands for itself."""
    out = []
    for ev, items in (events or {}).items():
        if not isinstance(items, list):
            continue
        at = _line(text, '"%s"' % ev) or _line(text, ev) or 1
        for item in items:
            if not isinstance(item, dict):
                continue
            group = isinstance(item.get("hooks"), list)
            for h in item["hooks"] if group else [item]:
                if not isinstance(h, dict):
                    continue
                cmd = str(h.get("command") or h.get("url") or "")
                escaped = json.dumps(cmd, ensure_ascii=False)[1:-1]
                line = (cmd and (_line(text, escaped, _line_offset(text, at))
                                 or _line(text, cmd, _line_offset(text, at)))) or at
                out.append({
                    "file": path, "line": line, "readers": readers, "scope": scope,
                    "source": source, "event": ev,
                    "matcher": str(item.get("matcher") or "") if group else "",
                    "command": cmd, "ours": _ours(h), "enabled": enabled,
                })
    return out


def _line_offset(text, line):
    "Character offset where 1-based LINE starts."
    off = 0
    for _ in range(line - 1):
        nl = text.find("\n", off)
        if nl < 0:
            break
        off = nl + 1
    return off


def _claude_style(path, readers, scope, source, enabled=True):
    text = _read(path)
    if text is None:
        return []
    try:
        data = json.loads(text)
    except ValueError:
        return [{"file": path, "line": 1, "readers": readers, "scope": scope, "source": source,
                 "event": "", "matcher": "", "command": "", "ours": False, "enabled": enabled,
                 "error": "not valid JSON"}]
    hooks = data.get("hooks") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    return _entries(path, text, hooks if isinstance(hooks, dict) else {}, readers, scope, source, enabled)


def _agy_file(path, scope, source):
    "agy's hooks.json: named specs, each {enabled?, Event: [...]}."
    text = _read(path)
    if text is None:
        return []
    try:
        data = json.loads(text)
    except ValueError:
        return [{"file": path, "line": 1, "readers": ["agy"], "scope": scope, "source": source,
                 "event": "", "matcher": "", "command": "", "ours": False, "enabled": True,
                 "error": "not valid JSON"}]
    out = []
    for name, spec in (data.items() if isinstance(data, dict) else []):
        if not isinstance(spec, dict):
            continue
        events = {k: v for k, v in spec.items() if k != "enabled"}
        out += _entries(path, text, events, ["agy"], scope, "%s · %s" % (source, name),
                        spec.get("enabled", True) is not False)
    return out


def _claude_plugins(settings_path):
    "hooks.json of each plugin claude's settings enable."
    data = {}
    text = _read(settings_path)
    try:
        data = json.loads(text) if text else {}
    except ValueError:
        pass
    found = []
    cache = os.path.expanduser("~/.claude/plugins/cache")
    for key, on in ((data.get("enabledPlugins") or {}).items() if isinstance(data, dict) else []):
        if not on or "@" not in key:
            continue
        name, market = key.split("@", 1)
        base = os.path.join(cache, market, name)
        try:
            versions = sorted((os.path.join(base, v) for v in os.listdir(base)),
                              key=os.path.getmtime, reverse=True)
        except OSError:
            continue
        for v in versions[:1]:
            hooks = os.path.join(v, "hooks", "hooks.json")
            if os.path.exists(hooks):
                found.append((hooks, name))
    return found


def _glob(pattern):
    import glob
    return sorted(glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(pattern)))


def inventory(projects=()):
    """Every hook claude, grok and agy would run, and every file looked in."""
    claude_readers = ["claude"] + (["grok"] if _grok_compat("claude") else [])
    places = []  # (kind, path, readers, scope, source, enabled)
    for scope, root in [("global", "~")] + [(p, p) for p in projects]:
        for name in ("settings.json", "settings.local.json"):
            path = os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(root), ".claude", name)
            places.append(("claude", path, claude_readers, scope, "claude " + name, True))
    for path, name in _claude_plugins(claude_settings()):
        places.append(("claude", path, ["claude"], "global", "plugin " + name, True))
    for path in _glob("~/.grok/hooks/*.json"):
        places.append(("claude", path, ["grok"], "global", "grok hooks", True))
    for path in _glob("~/.grok/hooks-disabled/*.json"):
        places.append(("claude", path, ["grok"], "global", "grok hooks (disabled)", False))
    for p in projects:
        for path in _glob(os.path.join(p, ".grok", "hooks", "*.json")):
            places.append(("claude", path, ["grok"], p, "grok hooks", True))
    if _grok_compat("cursor"):
        for scope, root in [("global", "~")] + [(p, p) for p in projects]:
            places.append(("claude", os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(root), ".cursor", "hooks.json"),
                           ["grok"], scope, "cursor hooks", True))
    places.append(("toml", os.path.expanduser("~/.grok/config.toml"), ["grok"], "global", "grok config", True))
    places.append(("agy", agy_hooks_file(), ["agy"], "global", "agy hooks.json", True))
    for path in _glob("~/.gemini/config/plugins/*/hooks.json"):
        places.append(("agy", path, ["agy"], "global", "agy plugin", True))
    for p in projects:
        places.append(("agy", os.path.join(p, ".agents", "hooks.json"), ["agy"], p, "agy hooks.json", True))
        for path in _glob(os.path.join(p, ".agents", "plugins", "*", "hooks.json")):
            places.append(("agy", path, ["agy"], p, "agy plugin", True))

    hooks, files = [], []
    for kind, path, readers, scope, source, enabled in places:
        exists = os.path.exists(path)
        files.append({"file": path, "readers": readers, "scope": scope, "source": source,
                      "exists": exists, "enabled": enabled})
        if not exists:
            continue
        if kind == "agy":
            hooks += _agy_file(path, scope, source)
        elif kind == "toml":
            text = _read(path) or ""
            data = _toml(text)
            if isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("hooks"), dict):
                hooks += _entries(path, text, data["hooks"], readers, scope, source)
            elif data is None and re.search(r"^\s*\[\[?hooks", text, re.M):
                hooks.append({"file": path, "line": _line(text, "hooks") or 1, "readers": readers,
                              "scope": scope, "source": source, "event": "", "matcher": "",
                              "command": "", "ours": False, "enabled": True,
                              "error": "has hooks this python3 cannot read (TOML needs 3.11)"})
        else:
            hooks += _claude_style(path, readers, scope, source, enabled)

    want = {"claude": list(CLAUDE_HOOKS), "grok": list(CLAUDE_HOOKS), "agy": list(AGY_HOOKS)}
    ghostherd = {}
    for cli, events in want.items():
        have = sorted({h["event"] for h in hooks
                       if h["ours"] and h["enabled"] and cli in h["readers"]})
        ghostherd[cli] = {"have": [e for e in events if e in have], "want": events}
    return {"hooks": hooks, "files": files, "ghostherd": ghostherd}


def cmd_hooks_list(args):
    inv = inventory([os.path.expanduser(p) for p in args.project or []])
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(inv, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    for cli, g in inv["ghostherd"].items():
        print("%-7s ghostherd %d/%d" % (cli, len(g["have"]), len(g["want"])))
    for h in inv["hooks"]:
        print("%-16s %-16s %-12s %s  %s:%s%s" % (
            ",".join(h["readers"]), h["event"], h["matcher"] or "-", h["command"][:60],
            h["file"], h["line"], "" if h["enabled"] else "  (disabled)"))
    return 0


def main(argv=None):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="herd",
        description="Ask another agent in the herd, or answer an ask.",
        epilog=__doc__.split("\n\n", 1)[1],
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest="cmd")
    p = sub.add_parser("ask", help="ask an agent; --wait for the answer")
    p.add_argument("to")
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--wait", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=DEFAULT_TIMEOUT)
    p.add_argument("--rounds", type=int, metavar="N",
                   help="how many times the taker may ask any one agent for this")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_ask)
    p = sub.add_parser("handoff",
                       help="hand work to another project's lead (a lead, or an agent "
                            "in a project with none)")
    p.add_argument("project", help="a path, its leaf name, or its store slug")
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--wait", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=DEFAULT_TIMEOUT)
    p.add_argument("--rounds", type=int, metavar="N",
                   help="how many times that lead may ask any one agent for this")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_handoff)
    p = sub.add_parser("reply", help="answer an ask")
    p.add_argument("id")
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_reply)
    for name, fn, what in (
        ("status", cmd_status, "an ask as it stands"),
        ("cancel", cmd_cancel, "withdraw an ask"),
    ):
        p = sub.add_parser(name, help=what)
        p.add_argument("id")
        p.set_defaults(fn=fn)
    sub.add_parser("list", help="the herd").set_defaults(fn=cmd_list)
    sub.add_parser("asks", help="open and recent asks").set_defaults(fn=cmd_asks)
    p = sub.add_parser("cost", help="what a task costs, through a lead and talking to an agent directly")
    p.add_argument("--days", type=int, default=7, help="the last N local days (7; at most 30)")
    p.add_argument("--project", metavar="P", help="one project's tasks: a path or its leaf name")
    p.add_argument("--tasks", action="store_true", help="list each task too, newest first")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_cost)
    p = sub.add_parser("remember", help="write a fact to the herd's shared memory")
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?")
    p.add_argument("--type", choices=("project", "feedback", "reference", "user"),
                   help="the fact's kind (default project)")
    p.add_argument("--name", metavar="SLUG",
                   help="its filename slug (default from the text); an existing one is updated")
    p.add_argument("--new", action="store_true",
                   help="keep it as a fact of its own though it says again one there")
    p.add_argument("--user", action="store_true", help="the store shared by every project")
    p.add_argument("--project", metavar="P",
                   help="another project's store: a path, its leaf name, or its slug")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_remember)
    p = sub.add_parser("recall", help="print the memory index, a fact by its name, or the facts most relevant to a query")
    p.add_argument("query", nargs="*")
    p.add_argument("--user", action="store_true", help="the user store, not the project's")
    p.add_argument("--project", metavar="P",
                   help="another project's store: a path, its leaf name, or its slug")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_recall)
    p = sub.add_parser("search", help="search what your project's past sessions said")
    p.add_argument("query", nargs="*")
    p.add_argument("--session", metavar="ID", help="read one session (its id, or the start of it)")
    p.add_argument("--at", metavar="TURN", type=int, default=0, help="from this turn (with --session)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_search)
    p = sub.add_parser("forget", help="remove a fact from shared memory")
    p.add_argument("name")
    p.add_argument("--user", action="store_true", help="from the user store")
    p.add_argument("--project", metavar="P",
                   help="another project's store: a path, its leaf name, or its slug")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_forget)
    p = sub.add_parser("promote",
                       help="propose promoting stable facts into the project's instruction file, "
                            "a check, or every project")
    p.add_argument("action", choices=("propose",))
    p.add_argument("--fact", action="append", metavar="NAME",
                   help="a fact to promote (repeatable)")
    p.add_argument("--file", metavar="PATH", help="the instruction file (e.g. CLAUDE.md)")
    p.add_argument("--lint", action="store_true",
                   help="propose a check made of the fact instead: the rule, JSON, on stdin")
    p.add_argument("--every-project", action="store_true",
                   help="move the fact to the user store, so every project has it -- its check and counts too")
    p.add_argument("--user", action="store_true", help="a fact of the user store (--lint only)")
    p.add_argument("--project", metavar="P",
                   help="the project's store: a path, its leaf name, or its slug")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_promote)
    p = sub.add_parser("memory",
                       help="migrate the existing claude memories into the store (reversible)")
    p.add_argument("action", choices=("plan", "migrate", "unmigrate"))
    p.add_argument("--project", action="append", metavar="PATH",
                   help="only this project (repeatable; default: all the herd knows)")
    p.add_argument("--user-name", action="append", metavar="SLUG",
                   help="a fact to route to the user store (repeatable)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_memory)
    p = sub.add_parser("relay",
                       help="hand an agent's work to a fresh agent on another CLI")
    p.add_argument("target")
    p.add_argument("kind", nargs="?", help="claude, grok or agy; omitted, the herd picks one with usage left")
    p.add_argument("--reason", help="why it is being relayed")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_relay)
    p = sub.add_parser("start",
                       help="start or reuse an agent in your project (lead only)")
    p.add_argument("kind", help="claude, grok or agy")
    g = p.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    g.add_argument("--worktree", nargs="?", const=True, default=False, metavar="BRANCH",
                   help="its own git worktree off HEAD (optionally naming the branch)")
    g.add_argument("--no-worktree", action="store_true",
                   help="run it in the main checkout, not a worktree")
    p.add_argument("--name", help="a name for it (default kind-project)")
    p.add_argument("--notes", help="its role / notes")
    p.add_argument("--new", action="store_true",
                   help="start a fresh agent; do not reuse an idle one")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_start)
    p = sub.add_parser("stop", help="stop an agent you started (lead only)")
    p.add_argument("name")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_stop)
    p = sub.add_parser("screens", help="saved agent screens from the log (read-only)")
    p.add_argument("--agent", help="only this agent")
    p.add_argument("--since", metavar="WHEN", help="3d / 2h / 90m, today, yesterday, or YYYY-MM-DD")
    p.add_argument("--why", help="only this trigger: limit, menu, mismatch, compaction, blocked, manual")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_screens)
    p = sub.add_parser("hook", help="run by a CLI's lifecycle hook, payload on stdin")
    p.add_argument("event", nargs="?")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_hook)
    p = sub.add_parser("lint", help="the checks: a CLI's PreToolUse hook, or `check COMMAND'")
    p.add_argument("action", choices=("check",))
    p.add_argument("text", nargs="?", metavar="COMMAND",
                   help="the command line to try (`-' or none: stdin)")
    p.add_argument("--rule", metavar="FILE", help="try this candidate rule alone (JSON)")
    p.add_argument("--cwd", metavar="DIR", help="as if run here (default: this shell's cwd)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_lint)
    p = sub.add_parser("guard", help="a guarded agy agent's PreToolUse hook, payload on stdin")
    p.add_argument("dir", help="the agent's guard directory")
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_guard)
    p = sub.add_parser("scrub-exec", help="run a command with only the allowed variables")
    p.add_argument("--allow", action="append", metavar="NAME", help="keep this name, or names matching this glob (repeatable)")
    p.add_argument("--scrub", action="append", metavar="REGEX", help="without --allow: drop names matching (repeatable)")
    p.add_argument("--keep", action="append", metavar="NAME", help="keep this name anyway (repeatable)")
    p.add_argument("cmd", nargs=argparse.REMAINDER)
    p.set_defaults(fn=cmd_scrub_exec)
    p = sub.add_parser("hooks", help="wire `hook' into claude, grok and agy, or list every hook")
    p.add_argument("action", choices=("install", "uninstall", "status", "list"))
    p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    p.add_argument("--project", action="append", help="also a project's own hooks (repeatable)")
    p.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: cmd_hooks_list(a) if a.action == "list" else cmd_hooks(a))
    args, extra = parser.parse_known_args(argv)
    # argparse settles an optional TEXT before it has read the options,
    # so `ask qa --wait -' or `ask qa --wait "text"' would leave the text
    # over -- the order the usage line suggests.
    if (len(extra) == 1 and getattr(args, "text", "") is None
            and (extra[0] == "-" or not extra[0].startswith("-"))):
        args.text = extra.pop()
    if extra:
        parser.error("unrecognized arguments: %s" % " ".join(extra))
    if not getattr(args, "fn", None):
        parser.print_help(sys.stderr)
        return 2
    try:
        return args.fn(args)
    except HerdError as exc:
        say(str(exc))
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
